---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EventCard from '../components/EventCard.astro';
import Actions from '../components/Actions.astro';
import { loadCalendarWithFeeds, upcoming } from '../lib/content.mjs';
const events = upcoming(await loadCalendarWithFeeds(), undefined, 120).filter((e) => (e.topics || []).includes('recycling'));
const swa = 'https://www.monongaliacountyswa.com';
const swaPhone = '304-292-3801';
---
<Base title="Trash, recycling and drop-off in Morgantown, WV" description="Pickup days, what goes in the curbside bin, and where to take electronics, paint, tires and other hard items in Morgantown and Monongalia County.">
  <h1>Trash, recycling and drop-off</h1>
  <p class="lede">Where to take trash, recycling and hard-to-dispose items in Morgantown and Monongalia County. Where we could not confirm a fact, we say so and give a phone number to call.</p>

  <h2>Find your pickup day</h2>
  <p>We could not find a public map or street list of pickup days. Inside Morgantown city limits, Republic Services is the hauler. Call the Monongalia County Solid Waste Authority at <a href="tel:3042923801">304-292-3801</a> and ask who serves your address and which day they come.</p>
  <p>A 2023 city checklist says to put trash and recycling out the same day, by 6 a.m. Check that with the hauler, since it may have changed.</p>

  <h2>What goes in the curbside bin</h2>
  <p>We could not find a current list from the city or hauler. The most recent clear guide we found is a <a href="https://www.republicservices.com/cms/documents/municipality/Morgantown/Morgantown-WV-service-guide-2019.pdf">2019 Republic Services guide for Morgantown</a>. It says glass food and beverage containers are accepted, and drinking glasses, ceramics and Pyrex are not. That guide is old, so confirm glass with the Solid Waste Authority at <a href="tel:3042923801">304-292-3801</a> before you rely on it.</p>

  <h2>Recycling drop-off sites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Single-stream recycling drop-off center</strong> (county, free): 34 Olin St., Industrial Park. Monday to Friday, 7:00 a.m. to 3:30 p.m. It moved here in August 2025, so check <a href="https://moncountyrecycling.com">moncountyrecycling.com</a> for current hours.
      <Actions place="34 Olin St, Industrial Park, Monongalia County, WV" /></li>
    <li><strong>Western Mon County Recycling Site</strong> (free, sorted by material): Arnettsville Community Association, 4120 Fairmont Rd., Morgantown. The county lists it as open 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.
      <Actions place="Arnettsville Community Association, 4120 Fairmont Rd, Morgantown, WV" /></li>
    <li><strong>Mountaineer Transfer Station</strong> (run by Republic Services, fee for recycling): call <a href="tel:3043687735">304-368-7735</a>. The county lists hours as Monday to Friday 5:30 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. and Saturday 7:00 to 11:00 a.m. It does not take tires.
      <Actions phone="304-368-7735" phoneLabel="Mountaineer Transfer Station" /></li>
    <li><strong>City residents:</strong> the county lists a Republic Services recycling event every second Saturday. Confirm the place and time with the hauler.</li>
    <li><strong>Paper shredding:</strong> PACE Enterprises at Mylan Park, <a href="tel:3043760036">304-376-0036</a>.
      <Actions phone="304-376-0036" phoneLabel="PACE Enterprises" /></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hard items</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Electronics:</strong> the county holds a free e-cycle event for county residents, with another planned for spring 2027. West Virginia also has a free take-back list for certain devices, linked from the <a href={`${swa}/recycling`}>county recycling page</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Tires:</strong> a state tire collection runs monthly in Morgantown, except December, January and February. The county's <a href={`${swa}/tires`}>tire page</a> has the yearly schedule.</li>
    <li><strong>Latex paint:</strong> the county plans a collection in 2027 but has no date yet. For oil-based paint and other household chemicals, the county points to the Morgantown Utility Board's yearly household hazardous waste day.</li>
    <li><strong>Batteries:</strong> we could not find a local drop-off program for batteries. Ask the Solid Waste Authority at <a href="tel:3042923801">304-292-3801</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Coming up</h2>
  {events.length ? events.map((e) => <EventCard e={e} />) : <p>No recycling events are on the calendar right now.</p>}
  <p><a href={`${swa}/events-1`}>County events page</a></p>

  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>Who to ask:</strong> Monongalia County Solid Waste Authority, 113 Mathieson Street, Suite 100, Morgantown. Phone <a href="tel:3042923801">304-292-3801</a>, email moncountyswa@gmail.com.</p>
    <Actions phone={swaPhone} phoneLabel="the Solid Waste Authority" place="113 Mathieson Street, Suite 100, Morgantown, WV" />
  </div>
  <p class="meta">Sources: <a href={swa}>monongaliacountyswa.com</a> (recycling, disposal, tires and latex paint pages), checked October 28, 2026, and the 2019 Republic Services guide linked above. Something out of date? <a href="https://github.com/david-shortman/mon-county-community-hub/issues/new?template=suggest-resource.yml">Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
